//@version=6
// =============================================================================
//  SMC / ICT / CRT SUITE  —  v8.2.1  (single-file build)
//  spec : INDICATOR_DEV_SPEC_BN.md   rules : BUILD_PROTOCOL_BN.md (R1 call-once, R2 one Cfg, R3 state in Ctx)
//  audit: FORENSIC_AUDIT_BN.md — this build implements stages 1, 2 and the cheap part of 3.
//  layers: L0 candle · L1 structure · L2 FVG/strength · L3 liquidity · L4 zones · L5 HTF · L6 setups · L7 trade
//  Feature-vector architecture: every layer runs ONCE per bar and writes flags; each setup = one boolean line.
//  Object budget (defaults): labels 200 sig + 30 liq = 230/500 · lines 100 struct + 30 liq + 12 HTF + 50 trade + 4 = 196/500
//  boxes 40 FVG + 60 zones = 100/500 · request.security 3/40 · plots 18/64 · all drawings FIFO-capped, oldest deleted first.
//
//  ── v8.2.0 CHANGELOG (forensic audit fixes) ───────────────────────────────────────────
//  C1  extreme-makers re-anchor on BOS/CHoCH; movePhase measured against the CURRENT leg,
//      not the all-time high/low (it used to read "RETRACEMENT" forever, killing M06/M07/M23).
//  C2  FVG detection gated on barstate.isconfirmed — the gap was being read off a live 3rd
//      candle, so every FVG (and the OB / chochReal / TP1 / score that hang off it) repainted.
//  C3  zone DETECTION decoupled from the "Show" toggles. d_ob / d_rcb / d_rjb / d_qm now only
//      control drawing; turning OB boxes off no longer disables M36/M37/M42/M45/M48.
//  C4  narrowed: f_conf score, the HTF/trend gate and the R:R test are all direction-only, so
//      they cannot single out one candidate — no candidate-chain refactor was needed. The one
//      real divergence (M10 in RETEST/BOTH mode moves the entry) now falls back to IMMEDIATE
//      instead of dropping the signal. Both-sides conflict and i_sigGap behaviour unchanged.
//  C5  majorHigh / majorLow re-anchor on a BOS that did not come off an LH/HL, and again on a
//      CHoCH, so the CHoCH reference can no longer stay `na` or drift decades behind price.
//  M1  BOS tie-break (a gap/outside bar could set bullBOS and bearBOS on the same bar).
//  M2  break flags resolved on CHoCH instead of being left latched.
//  M3  "OB: high-probability only" now suppresses the zone, not just its box.
//  M4  liquidity eviction is priority-based (keep pooled / PD / PW / session / near price).
//  M5  hidden-liquidity flags suppressed until `hiddenN + 1` bars exist.
//  M6  wick-dominance counters suppressed until 8 bars exist.
//  M7  sweep+BOS flags renamed to what they are; a genuine sweep+CHoCH arms M45 as the ★ form.
//  M8  the 4-factor "INCOMPLETE" verdict now costs a score point instead of being a dead note.
//  M10 arrivalMixed moved into Feat so it obeys the same 10-bar window as arrivalStrong.
//  M11 directional zone state (IDM, near-miss, 50%) cleared on flip / BRK conversion / PROP.
//  M12 rangeBrkDir cleared when a fresh range forms.
//  M14 trendline anchors expire by age and by distance from price.
//  M9  new input: which trend the HTF/trend gate reads (entering-bar default — this bar's own
//      BOS used to flip st.trend before the gate ran, so the gate passed trivially on BOS bars).
//  NEW Premium/Discount array (pdPct / inDiscount / inPremium were declared but never written).
//  NEW Session / killzone filter + Asia session SESH/SESL levels (the "SESH"/"SESL" branch in
//      the sweep classifier had no producer).
//  NEW dispScore / dispDir written and plotted; per-module hit counter in the strategy port.
//  DEAD removed: Cndl.dualTrap · Zone.propBar · Sx.dtTop · Feat.lastMoveFvg · Sig.sb · Sig.grade
//      · f_gradeSz (all were written-never-read or never written at all).
//  TOKENS the compiler counts code, not comments, and the build was 2677 tokens over the 100256
//      limit. Recovered by: replacing the tuple-threaded f_pick / f_try chains with one mutated
//      accumulator object per side (120 + 25 calls, same logic, ~1/3 the tokens), stripping 18
//      write-only type fields and their assignments, and REMOVING the seven modules the audit
//      flagged as effectively never firing - M55, M56, M57, M60, M61, M66, M71 (all default-OFF;
//      their state machines and Sx / Feat fields went with them).
//
//  ── v8.2.1 (live-chart review on BTCUSDT.P / BTCUSDT / EURUSD / ETHUSD, 1m) ────────────
//  R1  PD array read exactly "100% premium" on three of four charts: the range was built from the
//      CHoCH invalidation levels, which sit outside price in a trend. Range is now the last
//      completed swing, and price outside it is expansion (neutral), not saturated premium.
//  R2  TP1 had a floor but no ceiling, so 7R / 12R / 17R labels appeared on a 1m chart with empty
//      space in between. New input: Max R:R.
//  R3  PROP stamped 6-8 zones at once during a vertical leg. Now needs the 50% to have been hit
//      (price really was inside) and bounds the departure distance.
//  R4  KL scoring started at 2 of 3 criteria, so KL★ was everywhere and the zone gate was open on
//      almost every bar. Base 1 + four earned criteria, one of them the departure's own strength.
//  R5  `weak` / `not confirmed` zones could become the active zone (RJB▲ weak was tradable).
//  R6  Trendline slope cap, on top of the v8.2.0 age and distance caps.
//  R7  Overlapping same-kind zones are refreshed, not duplicated (three at one price was normal).
//  R8  A+ label cooldown bypass keeps a two-bar floor.
//  R9  HTF gate default STRICT → WARN: STRICT silenced both sides on an LTF/HTF conflict.
//
//  THIS FILE is the validation port of SMC_Suite_v8.2.1.pine (audit §6 stage 3.1): identical
//      detection, plus strategy entries so the Strategy Tester reports a real win rate and
//      expectancy. Keep the two in sync - the indicator is the source of truth. alertcondition()
//      is indicator-only and has been stripped; alert() still works.
//  STILL OPEN (audit §6 stages 3-4):
//      M13 f_bid uses a strict `>`, so equal base scores are settled by declaration order rather
//      than by merit — needs explicit priority tiers, which is the same refactor as unifying the
//      two scoring systems (base score picks the candidate, f_conf scores it) · cache the TP scans
//      · SMC_Suite_v8.2.1_strategy.pine is the companion port for real win-rate statistics.
// =============================================================================
strategy("SMC Suite v8.2.1 — validation strategy", "SMC Strat", overlay = true, max_bars_back = 500,
     max_labels_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_boxes_count = 500,
     default_qty_type = strategy.percent_of_equity, default_qty_value = 10, initial_capital = 10000,
     commission_type = strategy.commission.percent, commission_value = 0.02,
     calc_on_every_tick = false, process_orders_on_close = true)

// ── TYPES  (Cut-1 → lib/SMC_Types.pine) ──────────────────────────────────────
type Cfg
    float  pinWickMult     = 2.0
    float  pinWickRatioMin = 0.55
    float  dojiBodyMax     = 0.10
    float  largeRangeMult  = 1.5
    float  longWickRatio   = 0.50
    float  haramiBodyMax   = 0.60
    float  starProxATR     = 1.0
    float  ifcWickMult     = 2.0
    bool   ifcAnyColor     = false
    float  manipWickRatio  = 0.30
    int    swingLen        = 5
    int    rangeBarsThresh = 20
    float  wyckoffRangeMult = 1.5
    float  fvgMinATR       = 0.10
    string fvgMitMode      = "TOUCH"
    int    maxFvg          = 40
    int    fvgMaxAge       = 300
    int    minFVGForStrong = 1
    float  strongBodyEff   = 0.55
    float  strongMixMax    = 0.35
    float  strongSpeedMin  = 0.35
    int    maxMoveBars     = 150
    float  eqTolATR        = 0.10
    float  touchTolATR     = 0.15
    int    touchCooldown   = 3
    int    propWindow      = 10
    float  propImpATR      = 0.8
    float  runBodyMin      = 0.60
    float  runCloseMinATR  = 0.25
    float  sweepWickMin    = 0.40
    int    failedCloseBars = 2
    int    hiddenN         = 3
    float  hiddenWickMin   = 0.35
    int    extLookback     = 50
    int    maxLevels       = 30
    int    klLookLeft      = 50
    bool   klUseVol        = false
    int    sweepWindow     = 10
    float  rjbWickMin      = 0.50
    int    rjbConfirmBars  = 15
    int    qmMaxBars       = 60
    int    maxZones        = 30
    int    zoneMaxAge      = 500
    float  zoneMaxATR      = 3.0
    string gateMode        = "STRICT"
    int    sweepValidHTF   = 3
    int    candleLookback  = 3
    float  rejWickRatio    = 0.50
    float  volHighMult     = 2.0
    float  volLowMult      = 0.7
    int    pinCountMin     = 2
    int    dojiCountMin    = 2
    float  retestBodyRatio = 0.7
    float  nearZoneATR     = 3.0
    int    rangeLen        = 20
    float  rangeMaxATR     = 3.0
    int    armBars         = 30
    int    klMinCrit       = 3
    bool   rcbFibGate      = true
    bool   srTradable      = false
    bool   obHpOnly        = false
    int    maxLabels       = 200
    int    maxLines        = 100
    int    minGapBars      = 2

type Vis
    color  bull   = #089981
    color  bear   = #F23645
    color  neut   = #787B86
    color  pool   = #FF9800
    color  sr     = #787B86
    color  brk    = #9C27B0
    color  rcb    = #00BCD4
    color  rjb    = #FF9800
    color  qm     = #E91E63
    color  htf    = #2962FF
    color  inv    = #787B86
    color  txt    = #FFFFFF
    int    fillT  = 15
    int    boxT   = 85
    int    lineT  = 30
    int    boxMitT = 92
    bool   filled = true
    string sz     = "small"
    string zsz    = "small"
    float  offATR = 0.30

// L0 — candle anatomy (one per bar)
type Cndl
    float body        = 0.0
    float rng         = 0.0
    float upWick      = 0.0
    float dnWick      = 0.0
    float bodyRatio   = 0.0
    float upWickRatio = 0.0
    float dnWickRatio = 0.0
    bool  isBull      = false
    bool  isBear      = false
    bool  largeRange  = false
    bool  pinBull     = false
    bool  pinBear     = false
    bool  doji        = false
    bool  engulfBull  = false
    bool  engulfBear  = false
    bool  insideBar   = false
    bool  harami      = false
    bool  longWickRej = false
    bool  starBear    = false
    bool  starBull    = false
    bool  ifcBull     = false
    bool  ifcBear     = false
    bool  manipBull   = false
    bool  manipBear   = false

// L1 — structure output (one per bar)
type Struct
    bool   swingHigh = false
    bool   swingLow  = false
    bool   bullBOS   = false
    bool   bearBOS   = false
    bool   bullSweep = false
    bool   bearSweep = false
    bool   bullCHoCH = false
    bool   bearCHoCH = false
    bool   pbValidUp = false
    bool   pbValidDn = false
    bool   cisdBull  = false
    bool   cisdBear  = false
    string trend     = "RANGE"
    string movePhase = "IMPULSIVE"
    string wyckoff   = "ACCUMULATION"

// L2
type Fvg
    float top       = na
    float bottom    = na
    int   idx       = 0
    bool  isBull    = true
    bool  mitigated = false
    int   mitIdx    = 0
    box   bx        = na

type Move
    bool  strong   = false
    int   fvgCount = 0
    float bodyEff  = 0.0
    float mixed    = 0.0
    float speed    = 0.0
    float avgBody  = 0.0

// L3
type Liq
    float  price     = na
    int    idx       = 0
    bool   isHigh    = true
    string kind      = "BSL"
    bool   ext       = false
    int    touches   = 1
    int    lastTouch = 0
    int    pend      = 0
    bool   done      = false
    bool   pooled    = false
    string result    = ""
    line   ln        = na
    label  lb        = na

// L4
type Zone
    string kind      = "SR"
    bool   bull      = true
    float  top       = na
    float  bottom    = na
    int    idx       = 0
    int    touches   = 0
    int    lastTouch = 0
    bool   tapped    = false
    bool   fiftyHit  = false
    bool   broken    = false
    int    brokenAt  = 0
    bool   flipped   = false
    bool   sweepReq  = false
    bool   hp        = false
    bool   weak      = false
    bool   confirmed = true
    int    pendFvg   = 0
    int    kl        = 0
    float  idmLvl    = na
    bool   idmSwept  = false
    float  nearMiss  = na
    bool   nearSwept = false
    string obType    = ""
    bool   depStrong = false
    bool   prop      = false
    box    bx        = na

// R3 — ALL mutable state, one object
type Ctx
    array<Fvg>  fvgs
    array<Liq>  lv
    array<Zone> zones
    float curHigh = na
    float prevHigh = na
    int   curHighIdx = 0
    int   prevHighIdx = 0
    bool  hiBroken = false
    float curLow = na
    float prevLow = na
    int   curLowIdx = 0
    int   prevLowIdx = 0
    bool  loBroken = false
    float majorHigh = na
    int   majorHighIdx = 0
    float majorLow = na
    int   majorLowIdx = 0
    string trend = "RANGE"
    int   barsSinceEvt = 0
    float hiMakerHigh = na
    float hiMakerLow = na
    bool  pbUpArmed = false
    float loMakerLow = na
    float loMakerHigh = na
    bool  pbDnArmed = false
    bool  cisdUpSet = false
    float cisdUpOpen = na
    int   cisdUpBar = 0
    bool  cisdDnSet = false
    float cisdDnOpen = na
    int   cisdDnBar = 0
    bool  hidSSLprev = false
    bool  hidBSLprev = false
    int   sweptHighBar = -999
    int   sweptLowBar = -999
    bool  qmBullPend = false
    float qmBullLL = na
    int   qmBullAt = 0
    bool  qmBearPend = false
    float qmBearHH = na
    int   qmBearAt = 0
    float hCurHigh = na
    float hPrevHigh = na
    bool  hHiBroken = false
    float hCurLow = na
    float hPrevLow = na
    bool  hLoBroken = false
    float hMajorHigh = na
    float hMajorLow = na
    string hTrend = "NEUTRAL"
    int   hBarCount = 0
    int   sweepUpAt = -999
    int   sweepDnAt = -999
    int   pinBullInLeg = 0
    int   pinBearInLeg = 0
    int   dojiInLeg = 0
    int   greenRun = 0
    int   redRun = 0
    float upW1 = 0.0
    float upW2 = 0.0
    float dnW1 = 0.0
    float dnW2 = 0.0
    float upR1 = 0.0
    float upR2 = 0.0
    float dnR1 = 0.0
    float dnR2 = 0.0
    int   breakDir = 0
    float breakLvl = na
    int   breakBar = -999
    float breakLo = na
    float breakHi = na
    bool  lastDepStrong = false
    int   lastBOSBar = -999
    float lastBOSAvgBody = 0.0
    bool  chochReal = false
    bool  arrivalStrong = false
    int   arrivalBar = -999
    int   arrivalDir = 0
    float arrivalAvgBody = 0.0
    float arrivalMixed = 0.0
    float rangeHi = na
    float rangeLo = na
    bool  inRangePrev = false
    int   rangeBrkDir = 0
    int   rangeBrkBar = -999
    int   m41Dir = 0
    int   m41Bar = -999
    int   m45Dir = 0
    int   m45Bar = -999
    int   m46Dir = 0
    int   m46Bar = -999
    int   m48Dir = 0
    int   m48Bar = -999
    int   m52Dir = 0
    int   m52Bar = -999
    int   m54Stage = 0
    int   m54Bar = -999
    int   m54StageB = 0
    int   m54BarB = -999
    int   hidSSLBar = -999
    int   hidBSLBar = -999
    int   demandTouchBar = -999
    int   supplyTouchBar = -999
    int   bullFvgBar = -999
    int   bearFvgBar = -999
    string lastEvt = "—"
    int   lastEvtBar = -999
    bool  fiftyPrev = false
    int   brkTouch = 0
    int   swLoInLeg = 0
    int   swHiInLeg = 0
    float intLowB = na
    float intHighB = na
    int   intSwpBull = -999
    int   intSwpBear = -999

// L6 S–AB state machines (split from Ctx: UDT constructor limit 254 external elements, num/bool = 2 each)
type Sx
    int   dtDir = 0
    int   dtBar = -999
    float dtNeck = na
    int   m62Dir = 0
    int   m62Bar = -999
    float m62Lvl = na
    int   dbDir = 0
    int   dbBar = -999
    float dbLvl = na
    bool  dbNear = false
    int   tlSx1 = 0
    float tlSy1 = na
    int   tlSx2 = 0
    float tlSy2 = na
    int   tlSTouch = 0
    bool  tlSBroken = false
    int   tlRx1 = 0
    float tlRy1 = na
    int   tlRx2 = 0
    float tlRy2 = na
    int   tlRTouch = 0
    bool  tlRBroken = false
    int   m65Dir = 0
    int   m65Bar = -999
    float m65Ref = na
    int   m68Dir = 0
    int   m68Bar = -999
    int   ifcDir = 0
    int   ifcBar = -999
    float ifcHi = na
    float ifcLo = na
    int   brkTimeAt = 0
    int   m72Cnt = 0
    int   m72Wick = 0
    int   m72Dir = 0

// L2..L5 per-bar flags (feature vector) — setups read ONLY cd / st / ft
type Feat
    bool   newBullFvg = false
    bool   newBearFvg = false
    bool   dispBull = false
    bool   dispBear = false
    bool   lastDepStrong = false
    bool   sweptHigh = false
    bool   sweptLow = false
    bool   runUp = false
    bool   runDn = false
    bool   sweptPool = false
    bool   sweptMajor = false
    bool   runMajor = false
    string sweptKind = ""
    string sweptKindHi = ""
    string sweptKindLo = ""
    float  sweptPrice = na
    float  sweptPriceHi = na
    float  sweptPriceLo = na
    float  runPrice = na
    bool   hiddenSSL = false
    bool   hiddenBSL = false
    int    bslAbove = 0
    int    sslBelow = 0
    bool   atDemand = false
    bool   atProp   = false
    bool   newProp  = false
    bool   atSupply = false
    bool   atSupport = false
    bool   atResist = false
    string zKind = ""
    int    zTouches = 0
    bool   zSweepReq = false
    bool   zFifty = false
    bool   zIdm = false
    bool   zHp = false
    int    zKl = 0
    bool   zFlipped = false
    bool   zNearSwept = false
    bool   zDepStrong = false
    float  zTop = na
    float  zBottom = na
    bool   arrivalWeak = false
    bool   arrivalStrong = false
    // §M10 — the mixed ratio of the arrival leg. Was read straight off Ctx, where it kept the
    // verdict of the previous event long after the 10-bar arrival window had expired.
    float  arrivalMixed = 0.0
    string evtUp = ""
    string tipUp = ""
    string evtDn = ""
    string tipDn = ""
    string htfBias = "NEUTRAL"
    int    gateUp = 2
    int    gateDn = 2
    bool   htfSweepUp = false
    bool   htfSweepDn = false
    bool   htfManipBull = false
    bool   htfManipBear = false
    bool   htfRejBull = false
    bool   htfRejBear = false
    bool   volHigh = false
    bool   volSlopeNeg = false
    int    pinBullInLeg = 0
    int    pinBearInLeg = 0
    int    dojiInLeg = 0
    int    greenRun = 0
    int    redRun = 0
    bool   upWickInc = false
    bool   upWickDec = false
    bool   dnWickInc = false
    bool   dnWickDec = false
    bool   breakUp = false
    bool   breakDn = false
    int    breakAgo = 999
    bool   fakeBreak = false
    bool   insideOk = false
    bool   breakPinBull = false
    bool   breakPinBear = false
    bool   chochReal = false
    bool   retestValid = false
    bool   wickLowerDom = false
    bool   wickUpperDom = false
    bool   inRange = false
    bool   rangeShrink = false
    bool   atBullFvg = false
    bool   atBearFvg = false
    // §M7 — these are sweep + BOS, not sweep + CHoCH. The old names claimed CHoCH and a BOS
    // flips the trend before the CHoCH test runs, so the two can never coincide.
    bool   sweepBosBull = false
    bool   sweepBosBear = false
    bool   sweepChochBull = false
    bool   sweepChochBear = false
    bool   newObHp = false
    bool   enteredOb50 = false
    bool   tlSupValid = false
    bool   tlResValid = false
    bool   atTLsup = false
    bool   atTLres = false
    bool   incomplete = false
    int    brkTouches = 0
    int    swLoInLeg = 0
    int    swHiInLeg = 0
    bool   intSweptBull = false
    bool   intSweptBear = false
    bool   brkTimeOk = false
    int    cisdRel = 0
    string sessName = ""
    bool   sbSessOk = false
    float  pdPct = 0.5
    bool   inDiscount = false
    bool   inPremium = false
    int    dispScore = 0
    int    dispDir = 0

// L6 — the running best candidate of one side. The pick chain used to thread three values
// through 45 tuple assignments per side; mutating one object instead is the same logic at about a
// third of the compiled tokens, which is what brought the script back under the 100k limit.
type Best
    string n = ""
    int    s = 0
    string t = ""

// drawing — the winning label of one side, plus the priority rank that won it
type Tag
    string t = ""
    string p = ""
    color  c = na
    int    r = 0

// L6/L7 — one signal
type Sig
    string name  = ""
    int    dir   = 0
    float  entry = na
    float  sl    = na
    float  tp1   = na
    float  tp2   = na
    float  tp3   = na
    float  rr    = 0.0
    int    score = 0
    string note  = ""

// ── INPUTS  → one Cfg + one Vis (R2) ─────────────────────────────────────────
gA = "1 · General"
gC = "2 · Candle (L0)"
gS = "3 · Structure (L1)"
gF = "4 · FVG / Strength (L2)"
gL = "5 · Liquidity (L3)"
gZ = "6 · Zones (L4)"
gH = "7 · HTF (L5)"
gX = "8 · Setup filters (L6)"
gV = "9 · Visual · Colors"
gD = "10 · Show"

i_atrLen    = input.int(14,  "ATR length", minval = 1, group = gA)
i_swingLen  = input.int(5,   "Swing length (each side)", minval = 1, group = gA)
i_maxLabels = input.int(200, "Max labels", minval = 10, maxval = 500, group = gA)
i_maxLines  = input.int(100, "Max lines",  minval = 10, maxval = 500, group = gA)
i_minGap    = input.int(6,   "Min bars between labels (same side)", minval = 0, maxval = 20, group = gA)
i_lblMode   = input.string("Signals only", "Label density", options = ["Signals only", "Key events", "All events"], group = gA,
     tooltip = "Signals only = setup signals + zone boxes/lines (default — on a low timeframe anything more overlaps) · Key events = + real CHoCH, strong BOS, major sweeps, breakers, HTF · All events = every marker (CISD, FLIP, SWEEP REQ, warnings, hidden liquidity)")
tierAll = i_lblMode == "All events"
tierKey = i_lblMode != "Signals only"
i_setMode   = input.string("Custom (toggles)", "Setup master mode", options = ["Custom (toggles)", "Core only", "All on", "All off"], group = gA,
     tooltip = "Core only = the curated defaults regardless of toggles · All on = every module (heavy, cluttered) · All off = layers only, no setup signals")
// setup enable resolver: b = user toggle, core = curated default
f_en(b, core) =>
    i_setMode == "All on" ? true : i_setMode == "All off" ? false : i_setMode == "Core only" ? core : b

i_pinMult   = input.float(2.0,  "Pin bar wick ≥ N × body", minval = 0.5, step = 0.1, group = gC)
i_pinRatio  = input.float(0.55, "Pin bar wick/range min", minval = 0.1, maxval = 0.95, step = 0.01, group = gC)
i_dojiMax   = input.float(0.10, "Doji max body/range", minval = 0.01, maxval = 0.5, step = 0.01, group = gC)
